### Domain Test Descriptions
  - GATE 1 — Reconstruction identity vs the untouched oracle. SETUP: the five positive-parity anchor configs (kappa, gamma, y) used by the existing lens engine suite, each with its 2-decade production w window. Build ChangRefsdalChannels for each. OPERATION: on a dense w sampling of the window, compute F_reconstructed = sum_a S_a(w) H_a e^{i w tau_a} + e^{i w tau_c} E(w) from the new SACR-C accessor/per-image decomposition, and F_exact = channels.exact_total (the untouched oracle). EXPECTED: max over the window of |F_reconstructed - F_exact| / |F_exact| <= 1e-13 relative on ALL five anchors (report measured the _gauge telescoping identity at 2e-16). DIAGNOSTIC: plot |F_recon - F_exact|/|F_exact| vs w; a localized spike isolates a broken carrier phase or a mis-weighted S_a term.
  - GATE 2 — Greedy-oracle node count. SETUP: for each of the five anchors, build the dense TRUTH as a 506-point exact_total sampling over the 2-decade window. OPERATION: run a greedy oracle node-selection on the SACR-C envelope E(w) (repeatedly add the node that maximally reduces the max reconstruction error, using hindsight against the dense truth); count nodes N to reach eps = max|dF|/max|F| < 1e-3. EXPECTED: N <= 26 on every anchor (report: greedy-oracle 19-26, config-independent). DIAGNOSTIC: plot achieved eps vs N; the curve must cross 1e-3 by N=26. This gate isolates envelope smoothness from the production placement heuristic.
  - GATE 3 — Production LOO convergence + ceiling. SETUP: the five anchors (plus, optionally, the fold/cusp crossing configs). OPERATION: run the SHIPPED production LOO-adaptive placement (the WP2 loop, hard-coded stop 4e-3) and record the final node count N and the achieved envelope interpolation eps = max|dF|/max|F| against a dense exact_total truth. EXPECTED: eps < 1e-3 with N <= 48 on all anchors (report production range 30-44). DIAGNOSTIC: plot the LOO node placements over the window; failure to converge or clustering at the wrong scale flags a mis-demodulated envelope (tau_c error) or a broken LOO error estimate.
  - GATE 4 — S_a H_a boundedness at caustic crossings (F002 fixture independence). SETUP: fold and cusp crossing scenarios at eta = +/-0.002 on BOTH sides, constructed ONLY from geometry, operator, and _gauge — NEVER from channels.py — enforced by an AST import guard forbidding any channels.py import/name in the fixture builder (the idiom test_lensing_gauge.py already uses). OPERATION: evaluate max over images a and over the crossing w window of |S_a(w) H_a(w)|. EXPECTED: <= 2 (report measured <= 1.3; the S_a gate is provably more conservative than F008's switch where images merge). DIAGNOSTIC: plot |S_a H_a| vs w per image across the crossing; a divergence toward the caustic flags a switch separation still keyed on the wrong neighbour set (real-only vs the tau_c critical-carrier separation).
  - GATE 5 — Deep-band macro-magnification limit (F009). SETUP: a sheared positive-parity config (gamma != 0, e.g. gamma=0.2, kappa=0), evaluated at the low-w end of its window (tiny w, ~1e-8 across ~three decades 1e-8/1e-10/1e-12). OPERATION: compare |F_reconstructed| from the SACR-C reconstruction to the closed form 1/sqrt((1-kappa)^2 - gamma^2), computed INDEPENDENTLY (a literal closed form, NOT built from F_op/channels/geometry, per the F002 oracle-tautology trap). EXPECTED: < 1e-6 relative, and frequency-INDEPENDENT (a flat plateau across the three decades). DIAGNOSTIC: plot |F_recon| vs tiny w; a slope rather than a flat plateau signals a 1/w prefactor leak instead of the exact Gaussian macro limit.
  - F001 — Large-w carrier phase correctness. SETUP: a resolved multi-image config where w*max|tau_a - tau_c| reaches large values (thousands of radians) at the top of the window. OPERATION: compare the SACR-C reconstruction (carrier phases computed with mod-2*pi-reduced arguments before complex exp) against an independent high-precision (mpmath) direct e^{i w tau} reference at a handful of w points. EXPECTED: <= 1e-10 relative agreement (no float64 large-argument phase-precision loss). DIAGNOSTIC: plot phase error vs w*tau magnitude; error that grows with magnitude flags a missing or mis-placed mod-2*pi reduction. (mpmath is a test-only oracle, per FINDINGS F003 — do not add it as a runtime dependency.)
  - STRUCTURAL/TIMING GATE — node-count config-independence + public-entry speedup. SETUP: warm the lensed likelihood on a representative crown config. OPERATION: (a) record the LOO node count N on all five anchors; (b) time lnlike vs lnlike_bruteforce best-of-5, warm, single-thread. EXPECTED (structural leads): N <= 48 config-independent across anchors; lnlike faster than lnlike_bruteforce by a conservative margin against the PUBLIC entry points; secondary arithmetic-derived guard: warm best-of-5 lnlike <= 18 ms (the report's PROJECTED upper bound, not a machine-calibrated ceiling — the 10 ms owner target is the deferred envelope-surrogate lever, not this gate). DIAGNOSTIC: per-anchor node-count bar chart; any anchor exceeding 48 flags non-config-independent placement.
  - REGRESSION (confirm existing, do NOT re-author) — the shipped crown anchors must stay green at ORIGINAL tolerances after the construction change: test_lensing_likelihood.py RB-vs-brute (lnlike vs lnlike_bruteforce, RB_ATOL=1.5) on every lens regime; the near-cusp regression pin; the zero-noise floor anchors (the sheared macro-constant floors 0.1214/0.1307 per F009, and the unlensed 8.962e-3 + 2.676e-3 decomposition per F009); test_lensing_operator.py MacroMagnificationLimitTestCase; and the F008 crossing-scenario / label-continuity tests in test_lensing_gauge.py. EXPECTED: all green, unchanged. This is a run-and-confirm of existing suites, not new authoring.

